  "measurement_notes": [
    "Local equal-output microbenchmarks, with no timing assertions or end-to-end throughput claims.",
    "Borrowed join batches alternate baseline/refined order across three samples at each size. The baseline simulates prior eager row/payload cloning; this is not a whole-query comparison between commits.",
    "The fixture holds native integer and repeated wide string columns outside the measured statement allocator. Both paths build the same retained typed hash join state, with 1024-row inputs.",
    "Backing allocation counts and tracked allocator peaks do not measure process RSS.",
    "Existing lake/SQL benchmark cases are included for reproducibility; the two benchmark targets may overlap. Only the borrowed-batch case was added for this change.",
    "Parallel sort run creation and prefetched join builds are correctness-tested under shared budgets; their throughput is not quantified by the borrowed-batch benchmark."
  ],
